  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Welcome to Paper Flights!\nDive into a hand-drawn papercraft world where
    your trusty paper airplane navigates through dynamic classrooms, hallways, and
    office environments while dodging hazards and collecting gear!\n\nCore Gameplay
    & Mechanics\n- Seamless Side-Scrolling Environments: Implemented continuous background
    tiling (Background_1 and Background_2) with pixel-precision alignment for a smooth,
    endless hallway flight experience.\n- Fluid Flight Controls: Responsive movement
    mechanics designed specifically for agile dodging and precise firing in side-scrolling
    space.\n- Score & Currency Economy: Integrated coin collection mechanics (CoinItem.cs)
    linked directly to ScoreManager for tracking points and valuables on the fly.\n\nCombat
    & Boss Encounters\n- Standard & Homing Projectiles: Firing systems supporting
    standard straight shots alongside advanced homing rockets configured with optimized
    angle offsets (-90\xB0) to lock onto targets smoothly.\n- Wave Progression &
    Boss Fight: Defeat a targeted wave quota of mixed regular enemies before triggering
    an intense countdown sequence leading directly to the ultimate Boss confrontation.\n-
    Dynamic Enemy Spawning: Multi-config enemy spawner running independent, randomized
    interval loops for diverse enemy types to keep every run fresh and unpredictable.\n\nPower-Up
    System\n- Triple Shot: Triples your firepower spread to clear out crowded enemy
    lines quickly.\n- Shield: Grants temporary invulnerability backed by a custom
    visual indicator (ShieldVisual) wrapping your paper plane.\n- Magnet: Automatically
    pulls nearby coins straight toward your plane from a distance.\n- Rocket Launcher:
    Deploys high-impact homing rockets to clear obstacles.\n- Stacked Cooldown UI:
    Real-time multi-line text stack under the player tracking individual active timers
    (e.g., triple: 7s, magnet: 4s), automatically adding or removing lines dynamically
    as power-ups expire.\n\nAudio & Polish Updates\n- Crystal-Clear 2D Audio Architecture:
    Standardized sound effects across player actions, shooting, enemy hits, and coin
    pickups to play directly at camera coordinates, completely eliminating 3D distance
    attenuation muffling.\n- Interactive UI Sound Design: Fully integrated hover
    and click audio triggers across all main menu buttons (AboutUsButton, settings,
    navigation) powered by a centralized AudioManager.\n- Visual Polish: Added invulnerability
    flashing feedback for the player, dynamic rotation for pickups, and clean pause/game-over
    state managers.\n\nThank you for playing Paper Flights! More updates, levels,
    and features are coming soon."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
